  "test_contract": {
    "expected_observation": "Every coded horned species that lacks upper incisors has four stomach chambers and chews the cud, and every coded cud-chewer is one of those species.",
    "disconfirming_observation": "A horned species without upper incisors has a stomach that is not four-chambered, or a species chews the cud without being in that set.",
    "admissible_datasets": "Public species accounts that state horns or antlers, upper incisors, stomach chambers and cud-chewing for the pre-registered ungulates. A family account fills a trait only when the species account does not state it. Contrast clauses about other animals are not coded.",
    "inference_method": "Match the preregistered phrases in the subject clause of each sentence, with priority or exclusive mode as set per trait. Apply the minimum set and the counterexample rule."
  },
  "interpretation": "The quote identifies the horned animals that are not equally toothed in both jaws with the four-chambered cud-chewers. Antlers and ossicones count as horns because the claim's own examples include the stag and the test's giraffe is scored by the account's wording. A family sentence is used only as a fallback. Camelids are in the panel because they are the living cud-chewers outside the horned, four-chambered set; if their accounts do not state the four traits, the identity is untested rather than assumed.",
  "caveats": [
    "Phrase coding of prose can miss a trait that the account states in other words. Unstated is not a biological zero.",
    "The panel is twelve species, not every ungulate. One counterexample on the panel can refute a universal; agreement of the panel does not prove the universal beyond those accounts.",
    "Glossary popovers and the References section were excluded: a glossary example that names antlers is not a statement that the species has antlers, and a citation title is not a statement that the animal chews the cud. The registered token 'ruminant' does not match the plural 'ruminants' under the word-boundary rule, and that token was not added."
  ],
